{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And every woman wise of heart spun with her hands.</b> From here it follows that the wisdom of a woman is fitting only in spinning and in the diligent management of her household needs and the honor of her husband. Therefore our Rabbis of blessed memory forbade teaching Torah to daughters, as it is said (Deuteronomy 6:7) ״ושננתם לבניך״ — 'and you shall teach them to your sons' — and not to your daughters; and they said: whoever teaches his daughter Torah is as though he teaches her frivolity." "<b>And likewise</b> they expounded in Yoma, chapter 'The Goats of the Day of Atonement': ״וכל אשה חכמת לב בידיה טוו״ — 'and every woman wise of heart spun with her hands' — there is no wisdom for a woman except in the spindle."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:07:22.898540827Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}